WEBVTT

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:05.980
Those of us who were chosen to go and meet the people from the Ultima...

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:10.670
...left the Stellvia on the freighter Gagarin V.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:13.930
It's been one month since then.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.170
With only a ten-day wait until we arrive at the Ultima...

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:20.690
...our ship is going to be making a rendezvous...

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:24.330
...with the Clarke, a ship from the Odyssey.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars, Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて 飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Carry the unexpierence of the heart in the hands and go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて go far away

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
Urayamu koto ni Narete shimattara

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
If you have experienced the envy

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
羨む事に 慣れてしまったら

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Hokoreru jibun ga Toozakatteku

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Your proud self will go far away

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
誇れる自分が 遠ざかってく

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Mienai tsubasa de habataku no fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Flapping the invisible wings to fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
見えない翼で羽ばたくの fly higher

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
Yume wo egaku no wa hito ni umareta kara

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
I'm imaging dreams because I was born a "person"

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
夢を描くのは「人」に生まれたから

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Carry the unexperienced of the heart in the hands

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
Anata to nara Yowai jibun wo sarakedashite hashiridaseru no

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
If I were with you, I'd start running, exposing my weak self

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
あなたとなら 弱い自分をさらけ出して走り出せるの

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
Mirai yo dou ka Mugen ni tsuzuke go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
The future! Somehow continues to the infinity, go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
未来よどうか 無限に続け go far away

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:05.770
Episode Sixteen: 
In Doubt

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:15.320
10 days until arrival at the Ultima

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:15.410
I'm surprised that the guys from the Odyssey caught up.

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:17.450
They launched quite a while after we did.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:19.920
They're probably going really fast.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:22.820
So I guess they're less concerned about the welfare of the Ultima...

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:25.240
And more concerned about the Stellvia's battle strength, right?

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.090
That's probably it.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:29.420
Captain, there is an incoming message from the Clarke.

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:30.970
All right, put it on.

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:36.030
Hello, Mr. Shirogane, long time no see.

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:38.050
Yo, not since we graduated, right?

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.430
So you're the commander over there?

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:43.780
Well, aren't you supposed to be a teacher, upperclassman?

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:46.560
I'm sure we both have a lot to deal with.

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:47.740
That's true.

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:54.770
By the way, the students say that they want to make a courtesy call...

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:56.910
A courtesy call?

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:19.810
Oh! It's the people who pissed me off during the astroball games!

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.650
Welcome to the Gargarin V.

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:27.960
Long time no see, Kent Austin.

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:32.130
The makeup of your team's members has changed quite a bit.

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:33.340
What happened to Machida?

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:37.130
A few minor things came up.

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:39.440
Shima Katase...

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:41.610
...you already know.

00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:43.610
What's happened to her?

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.160
She lost a game.

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:49.070
That's Kouta Otoyama, our miracle rookie.

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:50.290
Nice to meet you.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:59.310
But you guys coming here means...

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:03.310
...that the Stellvia isn't the only place that works its students hard.

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:05.450
Well, unlike the Earth...

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:09.260
...Mars has had several confirmations of the unidentified flying objects.

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:11.690
And because we're so busy fortifying our defenses...

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:13.330
...we could use anyone's help, even a cat's.

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:16.110
Defense, in other words, will become an offense.

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:18.870
No matter from who and how you plan on protecting yourselves...

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:19.900
Now, now, Naji.

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:20.590
Hey!

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:21.600
What's up?

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:24.260
Ritsuo Syoujin!

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:24.810
Hmm?

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:28.310
Could it be that those two are going out?

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:29.870
Do you mean Katase and Otoyama?

00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:31.380
Who else is there?

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:33.950
Katase!
Yes?

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:36.670
Are you going out with Otoyama?

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:40.280
Yes!

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:41.270
So it seems.

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:45.430
By the way...

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:48.580
...would it be all right for us to look at that secret weapon up close?

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:49.650
The secret weapon?

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:51.300
Don't play dumb.

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:54.370
The giant robot is connected to the stern of the ship, right?

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.110
Is this an order from the top?

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:11.770
We'd like to inspect it.

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:21.590
Commander Shirogane.

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:25.860
The students from the Odyssey say they would like to inspect the Infinity.

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:27.770
Would you please give us permission?

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:30.640
Yes, sir, I understand.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:33.580
It looks like it's all right. Do you want to go look at it now?

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:37.570
Sorry about this.

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:40.380
Don't worry about it.

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:52.240
3 days until arrival at the Ultima

00:05:57.350 --> 00:05:59.810
Hey, there's no use in just sitting here silently...

00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:01.420
...waiting for an answer from over there.

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:02.930
So why don't you relax?

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:06.950
But then I wouldn't be talking with Rinna, would I?

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:11.370
But that's no reason to sit and stare at the screen while you wait, right?

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:13.660
Shima-chan is unexpectedly stubborn.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:16.150
There's a time lag, so this is useless.

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:18.310
Oh, shut up, you two.

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:20.360
Oh, there it is!

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:21.700
Isn't it, though?

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:24.930
My father is so mean! Just recently, he...

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:27.250
Rinna?

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:29.270
I wonder what that was? All of a sudden...

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:32.370
Rinna?

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:34.840
Rinna. Rinna!

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:37.310
That was the emergency alarm we just heard, wasn't it?

00:06:39.070 --> 00:06:40.090
Rinna...

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:42.630
There is no response from the Ultima...

00:06:42.780 --> 00:06:44.160
...neither by electromagnetic wave nor by laser.

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:46.910
Push up the schedule for making the rendezvous with the Ultima.

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:48.390
Contact the Clarke, too!

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:49.170
Roger!

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:51.940
Damn it, and we're so close to arriving, too.

00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:08.830
Where's Katase?

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:11.400
In the communications room, as usual.

00:07:12.010 --> 00:07:13.410
She won't listen to anything I say, so...

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:15.710
So you're already being controlled by her, are you?

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:16.550
What?

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:26.030
She's all right, I'm sure of it...

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:33.430
20 hours later

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:32.660
Rinna...

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:34.420
Commander...

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:35.660
Commander!

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:37.500
What's wrong?

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:40.030
There is an object approaching from in front of us.

00:07:40.490 --> 00:07:40.980
What is it?

00:07:41.450 --> 00:07:42.950
We're currently confirming it.

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:44.740
It's...

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:47.030
We've made confirmation.

00:07:47.550 --> 00:07:49.230
It's the Ultima's residential block!

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:50.060
Wha...?

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:51.510
I'm putting it on the monitor.

00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:57.260
Has it been attacked?

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:58.380
Commander!

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:00.390
Do a U-turn and dock with it.

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:02.930
Contact the Clarke and tell it to continue on, just as it is.

00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:03.710
Roger!

00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:16.730
Please continue forward without hurrying.

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:18.260
Calm down.

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:20.600
I'm sorry, please let us through. Excuse us.

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:28.730
What happened?

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:30.480
What is this?

00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:32.170
Rinna... Rinna...

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:33.610
It's all right now.

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:35.780
Get a hold of yourself, come on.

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:36.940
Rinna!

00:08:39.340 --> 00:08:42.350
Thank goodness, Rinna. You're all right.

00:08:42.690 --> 00:08:44.170
I was so worried!

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:46.280
Shipon...

00:08:48.740 --> 00:08:49.950
It's Shipon!

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:54.200
I... I thought I might...

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:55.790
...never see you again.

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:02.050
Rinna...

00:09:12.590 --> 00:09:13.110
Um...

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:15.590
Exactly what happened?

00:09:16.060 --> 00:09:16.640
That's correct.

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:20.490
The unidentified flying objects came and attacked us all of a sudden.

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:23.900
They hadn't made any direct contact up until then...

00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:25.230
So why...

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:26.940
We don't know.

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:29.940
In any case, one of the enemy units attached itself to the Ultima...

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:32.690
...and began to take control of the entire station.

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:35.120
And that is why we escaped.

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:37.180
But the commander and the heads of the science department...

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:38.330
...are still in the main block.

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:40.120
They're still back there?

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:41.280
Yes.

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:45.560
They said they absolutely had to complete their analysis...

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:47.870
...of the incoming astronomical phenomenon.

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:51.260
That would be the himo-shaped astronomical thing, right?

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:52.090
Yes.

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:55.470
What's going on?

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:12.880
These are the images that the Clarke, which went ahead, sent back.

00:10:13.690 --> 00:10:15.890
There are two units docked with the Ultima...

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:18.000
...and three units flying about the surrounding area.

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:21.300
A total of five units of unknown origin have been confirmed.

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:24.160
At this time, most of the people have managed to escape...

00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:26.130
...but there are still five people left onboard.

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:28.120
Including Commander Roskov.

00:10:29.570 --> 00:10:32.810
Your goal is to cooperate with the formation from the Clarke...

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:35.580
...and allow the rescue ship I'll be aboard to infiltrate the Ultima.

00:10:35.930 --> 00:10:38.670
While we are rescuing the five remaining people in the main block...

00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:41.140
...you will be drawing away the attention of these ships.

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:44.780
No matter what, the goal of this mission is life-saving.

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:47.360
Avoid unnecessary combat to the best of your ability.

00:10:47.900 --> 00:10:48.450
Got it?

00:10:48.770 --> 00:10:49.390
Roger!

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:54.410
Shipon!

00:10:58.280 --> 00:10:59.730
What's wrong, Rinna?

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:01.410
Please, Shipon!

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:05.340
Please ask Mr. Shirogane to take me with you!

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:08.350
My papa is still on the Ultima.

00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:13.230
I promised him that I would go and get him, no matter what!

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:14.880
That's why...

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:16.960
That's why...

00:11:17.980 --> 00:11:18.810
Rinna...

00:11:20.090 --> 00:11:21.450
But it's going to be dangerous...

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:24.800
Even the upperclassmen in the Big Four are standing by.

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:28.070
And in the first place, there's no unit for you to pilot.

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:29.020
But...

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:30.260
It'll be all right!

00:11:31.070 --> 00:11:33.940
We'll be sure to rescue your father!

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:37.090
I'm telling you, believe in the miracle, ejected girl!

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:38.100
Okay?

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:46.980
Launch the Infinity, too.

00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:47.850
Roger.

00:12:05.310 --> 00:12:06.760
Infinity, launch!

00:12:07.310 --> 00:12:07.940
Launch!

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:30.850
Ultima Main Room

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:33.590
It's an unusually large piece...

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:38.070
It will take several hours to analyze the whole thing.

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:39.290
I see.

00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:42.610
All I can say is, do your best, but...

00:12:43.250 --> 00:12:44.100
I understand.

00:12:47.180 --> 00:12:50.540
The crevasse in space, the "Cosmic Fracture."

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:55.740
No matter what, we must gather accurate data...

00:12:56.550 --> 00:12:57.740
There's no time left.

00:12:58.110 --> 00:13:00.650
Commander! A large number of objects approaching!

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:02.250
We believe they're the rescue party.

00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:04.850
So they've finally arrived?

00:13:17.110 --> 00:13:18.120
Members from the Odyssey...

00:13:19.080 --> 00:13:21.450
...I'm Shirogane of the Stellvia, and I will be leading this mission.

00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:23.070
I'm looking forward to working with you.

00:13:23.330 --> 00:13:25.010
We're looking forward to working with you, too.

00:13:25.930 --> 00:13:28.820
We've heard about you from our team, Commander Shirogane.

00:13:29.860 --> 00:13:30.440
Really?

00:13:31.050 --> 00:13:33.880
The details of the mission are just as we discussed previously.

00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:34.920
Roger!
Roger!

00:13:36.020 --> 00:13:37.670
Infinity, you'll be our escort.

00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:38.230
Yes, sir!
Yes, sir!

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:56.150
Those are the unidentified units?

00:13:56.470 --> 00:13:57.250
That's right.

00:13:57.570 --> 00:13:59.760
Right now, don't think about who they belong to.

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:01.850
Just concentrate on the mission.

00:14:02.140 --> 00:14:02.600
Roger.

00:14:05.890 --> 00:14:06.210
Go!

00:14:13.640 --> 00:14:15.210
I'm counting on you, Spears.

00:14:23.790 --> 00:14:25.730
All right, it's time to start playing tag.

00:14:37.670 --> 00:14:39.120
There's no reaction whatsoever.

00:14:41.260 --> 00:14:42.240
We're going in, too.

00:14:51.640 --> 00:14:52.760
It's still no use!

00:14:55.460 --> 00:14:57.190
The mission has still just begun.

00:14:57.660 --> 00:15:00.290
In any case, just keep going and don't let up.

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:01.210
Roger!
Roger!

00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:04.440
Approach the unit that's attached to the Ultima, too.

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:05.480
Roger!

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:06.620
It'll be all right.

00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:08.330
Right.

00:15:09.710 --> 00:15:11.360
Second squadron, third squadron!

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:13.320
We're going to follow them in, too!

00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:32.240
Damn it!

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:33.740
Spears!

00:15:38.340 --> 00:15:39.210
Why, you!

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:42.740
Are you saying you don't have any interest in little guys like us?

00:15:42.850 --> 00:15:43.570
Spears!

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:46.470
What'll happen if you start to do foolish things yourself?

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:47.710
But, Commander...!

00:15:48.110 --> 00:15:50.020
This is getting us nowhere!

00:15:57.450 --> 00:16:00.060
Commander Shirogane, at this rate...

00:16:00.550 --> 00:16:02.110
What? What's wrong?

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:03.590
Please give the order to attack!

00:16:04.340 --> 00:16:04.860
No!

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:08.360
If they're not moving, that's actually better for us.

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:10.930
Continue your approaches, just like that.

00:16:11.160 --> 00:16:11.910
But...

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:13.130
Now listen!

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:15.960
We're going to come in through their blind spot...

00:16:16.020 --> 00:16:17.780
...and somehow dock with the main block.

00:16:18.510 --> 00:16:19.290
I see...

00:16:19.430 --> 00:16:19.850
That's right!

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:23.620
The primary purpose of our current mission is rescue...

00:16:24.090 --> 00:16:27.120
...not to needlessly expose you pilots to danger.

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:29.490
Don't be impatient, just continue your diversions.

00:16:30.510 --> 00:16:31.140
Roger.

00:16:34.090 --> 00:16:36.780
Mr. Shirogane is cool, isn't he?
Yeah.

00:16:40.340 --> 00:16:42.130
All right, we're going to board the Ultima!

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:42.910
Roger!
Roger!

00:16:55.840 --> 00:16:56.760
Break away quickly!

00:16:57.250 --> 00:16:57.800
Roger!

00:17:01.100 --> 00:17:02.160
